1
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:43,500
How far would you go to escape the past?

2
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:21,000
The Human Stain is a drama, romance film directed by Robert Benton.

3
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:58,500
Coleman Silk is a worldly and admired professor who loses his
job after unwittingly making a racial slur.

4
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:36,000
To clear his name, Silk writes a book about the events with his friend and colleague Nathan
Zuckerman, who in the process discovers a dark secret Silk has hidden his whole life.

5
00:33:07,500 --> 00:33:13,500
All the while, Silk engages in an affair with Faunia Farley, a younger woman whose
tormented past threatens to unravel the layers of deception Silk has constructed.

6
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:51,000
Coleman Silk, played by Anthony Hopkins.

7
00:46:22,500 --> 00:46:28,500
Faunia Farley, played by Nicole Kidman.

8
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
Lester Farley, played by Ed Harris.

9
00:59:37,500 --> 00:59:43,500
Nathan Zuckerman, played by Gary Sinise.

10
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:21,000
Young Coleman Silk, played by Wentworth Miller.

11
01:12:52,500 --> 01:12:58,500
Steena Paulsson, played by Jacinda Barrett.

12
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:36,000
The Human Stain is a 2003 American drama film directed by Robert Benton.

13
01:26:07,500 --> 01:26:13,500
Its screenplay, by Nicholas Meyer, is based on the
novel of the same name by Philip Roth.

14
01:32:45,000 --> 01:32:51,000
The film stars Anthony Hopkins, Nicole Kidman, Gary Sinise, and Ed Harris.

15
01:39:22,500 --> 01:39:28,500
The tone is dark and emotional.
